    "structure": {
      "#post": "green post pieces (cap + shaft segments visible between/below the signs), drawn first",
      "#sign-top": "WOODWARD sign: path.plate (green fill + same-colour round-join stroke for softened corners) + path.ink (white border frame + stencil letters)",
      "#sign-bottom": "SPORTS sign: path.plate + path.ink, drawn above #sign-top (it overlaps the top sign's lower-right corner)",
      "#network": "white NETWORK wordmark (path.word) + two sets of tapered speed lines (path.lines); sits on the post below the signs"
    },
    "pivots_viewbox_units": {
      "post_center_x": 248.6,
      "sign-top": [
        248.6,
        129.7
      ],
      "sign-bottom": [
        248.6,
        313.8
      ],
      "post_base": [
        248.6,
        500
      ],
      "post_x_range": [
        214.8,
        282.5
      ]
    },
    "animation_hint": "Inline the SVG (fetch img/logo.svg and inject, or paste) so the groups are addressable. For a swing-in: '#sign-top,#sign-bottom{transform-box:view-box}' then '#sign-top{transform-origin:248.6px 129.7px}' '#sign-bottom{transform-origin:248.6px 313.8px}' and animate rotate(-12deg)->rotate(0) with a springy cubic-bezier; '#post{transform-origin:248.6px 500px}' scaleY(0)->1 first; '#network' fade/slide last. Pivots sit on the post centre so the post stays covered while the signs swing (small rotations, <15deg, look best). The SVG uses fill attributes (not classes in a <style>), so page CSS can recolour e.g. '#network{fill:...}'.",
    "light_background": "The original logo's NETWORK + speed lines are white and disappear on white/light backgrounds (same as the source art). Use img/logo-on-light.svg there (NETWORK in brand green), or set #network{fill:#087656}.",
    "bytes": {
      "svg": 37561
    },
    "source_url": "https://woodwardsports.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Woodward-Sports_logo.webp"
  },
